# Connect ↔ Cobalt ↔ yt-session checklist (Render)

## Cobalt service (`cobalt-yt`)
```
COBALT_API_KEY=7699759e-fe6a-49a9-9589-cc22baf0188e
API_AUTH_REQUIRED=1
CORS_WILDCARD=1
YOUTUBE_COOKIES_B64=<same as Connect, no quotes>
YOUTUBE_SESSION_SERVER=https://yt-session-75x3.onrender.com/
YOUTUBE_SESSION_INNERTUBE_CLIENT=WEB_EMBEDDED
```
Do **not** set `COOKIE_PATH` or `COBALT_API_URL` on Cobalt.

## yt-session service
- Health Check Path: `/health`
- Plan: **Starter or higher** (Chromium often fails on Free)
- After deploy, wait until `GET /token` returns JSON with `potoken`

## Connect server (local + Render)
```
COBALT_API_URL=https://cobalt-yt.onrender.com
COBALT_API_KEY=7699759e-fe6a-49a9-9589-cc22baf0188e
YT_DL_PREFER_COBALT=true
YT_DL_COBALT_ONLY=false
YOUTUBE_COOKIES_B64=<cookies>
```

`YT_DL_COBALT_ONLY=false` is required so Connect still downloads via yt-dlp when Cobalt hits YouTube bot checks.
